    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00001",
      "text": "On May 20, 2021, a Singaporean container ship X-Press Pearl had caught fire on the Laccadive Sea, 18 kilometres off the west coast of Sri Lanka near the capital Colombo. After a week of firefighting efforts, the vessel was declared a total loss and had started to sink releasing burnt debris. The X-Press Pearl was carrying 1,486 containers of chemicals and cosmetics, including 28 containers of plastic pellets and 25 tonnes of extremely combustible nitric acid and sodium hydroxide, which were loaded from a port in Gujarat, India. Apart from the burnt debris, it also threatens an oil spill as the ship had more than 300 tonnes of fuel in its tanks.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 652,
      "source_links": [
        "https://edition.cnn.com/2021/06/02/asia/sri-lanka-ship-sinking-intl-hnk/index.html",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laccadive_Sea",
        "https://news.yahoo.com/sri-lankas-sinking-ship-know-084254742.html",
        "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2021/6/2/sri-lanka-disaster-feared-as-fire-hit-chemical-cargo-ship-sinks",
        "https://www.marinetraffic.com/en/ais/details/ships/shipid:6450863/mmsi:563118200/imo:9875343/vessel:X_PRESS_PEARL",
        "https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2021/may/31/sri-lanka-environmental-disaster-cargo-ship-burns-for-days-video"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00002",
      "text": "Explosions were heard as the ship burnt in the fire for the past two weeks and the burnt debris and oil residues have already caused massive damage to the nearby Sri Lankan coastline. The magnitude of the damage makes it one of the worst environmental disasters of Sri Lanka.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 654,
      "body_end": 929,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.msn.com/en-in/news/world/with-cargo-ship-sinking-sri-lanka-faces-one-of-worst-environmental-disasters-in-decades/ar-AAKEFll",
        "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/31/sri-lanka-faces-disaster-burning-ship-spills-chemicals-beaches"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00003",
      "text": "Journalist Rangana Shamil Fernando shares footage of the sinking ship recorded by the Sri Lankan Navy:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 931,
      "body_end": 1033,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00004",
      "text": "Reportedly, the ship had a nitric acid leak that had started on May 11 and the vessel arrived in Sri Lanka asking for help after other nearby ports refused to allow it in with its leak.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 1035,
      "body_end": 1220,
      "source_links": [
        "https://news.yahoo.com/sri-lankas-sinking-ship-know-084254742.html"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00005",
      "text": "Journalist Azzam Ameen shares Sri Lankan Air Force footages:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 1222,
      "body_end": 1282,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00006",
      "text": "The Sri Lankan navy has rescued 25 crew members from the cargo ship after explosions ripped off sections. The Indian navy assisted in controlling the fire breakout.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 1284,
      "body_end": 1448,
      "source_links": [
        "http://www.adaderana.lk/news/74116/explosion-in-x-press-pearl-on-fire-off-colombo-25-crew-members-rescued",
        "http://www.dailynews.lk/2021/05/26/local/250160/options-run-out-mv-x-press-pearl"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00007",
      "text": "Environmental damage",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 7,
      "body_start": 1450,
      "body_end": 1470,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h4",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00008",
      "text": "Waves of microplastics and charred debris from the burning vessel have already reached the nearby popular beaches of Negombo in the past two weeks.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 8,
      "body_start": 1472,
      "body_end": 1619,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.bbc.com/news/av/world-asia-57292558",
        "https://www.marineinsight.com/shipping-news/photos-plastic-waste-from-blazing-cargo-ship-wash-up-on-sri-lankan-coast/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00009",
      "text": "Ocean Conservationist Maleesha Gunawardana tweeted:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 9,
      "body_start": 1621,
      "body_end": 1672,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00010",
      "text": "The Sri Lankan authorities have banned fishing on an 80-kilometre stretch of coast which affected over 5000 fishing boats and the livelihoods of fishermen depended on them.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 10,
      "body_start": 1674,
      "body_end": 1846,
      "source_links": [
        "http://www.adaderana.lk/news/74116/explosion-in-x-press-pearl-on-fire-off-colombo-25-crew-members-rescued"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00011",
      "text": "Sri Lankan environmental conservation organisation the Pearl Protectors tweeted regular updates about the disaster.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 11,
      "body_start": 1848,
      "body_end": 1963,
      "source_links": [
        "https://pearlprotectors.org/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00012",
      "text": "The organisation also highlighted the consequences in a statement on Facebook:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 12,
      "body_start": 1965,
      "body_end": 2043,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.facebook.com/182685099222955/posts/931215907703200"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00013",
      "text": "> Large areas of the Western Province coast have been affected due to the recent MV X-Press Pearl ship accident. Due to the complexity of its cargo, several environmental challenges have arisen. These include high toxic levels both at sea and on the coast. A bunk oil spill, ashes and ship debris at sea and on the shorelines, high amounts of plastic pellets spilled onto the ocean now covering large swaths of coastline along the western side of Sri Lanka, toxic fumes mixed with monsoon rains resulting in toxic rain and poor air quality.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 13,
      "body_start": 2045,
      "body_end": 2585,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00014",
      "text": "Hemantha Withanage, the Executive Director of Centre for Environmental Justice Sri Lanka wrote on Groundviews:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 14,
      "body_start": 2587,
      "body_end": 2697,
      "source_links": [
        "https://groundviews.org/2021/06/03/the-x-press-pearl-fire-a-disaster-of-unimaginable-proportions/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00015",
      "text": "> Although the impact on biodiversity is yet to be assessed, there are several reefs located in the area and the fauna and flora associated with the reefs will be seriously affected. Turtles, moray eel and stingray have washed up on beaches.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 15,
      "body_start": 2699,
      "body_end": 2940,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00016",
      "text": "Rescue efforts",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 16,
      "body_start": 2942,
      "body_end": 2956,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h4",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00017",
      "text": "Hundreds of members of armed forces and other personnel are assisting the cleanup to remove debris in dozens of locations across the coast.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 17,
      "body_start": 2958,
      "body_end": 3097,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.msn.com/en-xl/asia/srilanka/coastal-clean-up-operations-carried-out-expeditiously-ministry/ar-AAKEp1n"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00018",
      "text": "Journalist Roel Raymond Tweets:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 18,
      "body_start": 3099,
      "body_end": 3130,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00019",
      "text": "The Sri Lankan authorities are devising strategies to mitigate the environmental damage and has started an investigation into the cause of the accident.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 19,
      "body_start": 3132,
      "body_end": 3284,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00020",
      "text": "A video released by the Marine Environment Protection Authority of Sri Lanka on Facebook shows how the small plastic parts from the sinking MV X-Press Pearl ship are being painstakingly removed.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 20,
      "body_start": 3286,
      "body_end": 3480,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.facebook.com/182685099222955/posts/932416117583179"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00021",
      "text": "However, the fear is that the currents will take the debris to the West coast of Sri Lanka. Charitha Pattiaratchi, Professor of the University of Western Australia, shared a projection of the path of the plastic nurdles:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 21,
      "body_start": 3482,
      "body_end": 3702,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.facebook.com/charitha.pattiaratchi/posts/10159500446929042"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00022",
      "text": "Meanwhile, the Sri Lankan authorities decided to sue the owners of X-Press Pearl for marine pollution and launched an investigation.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 22,
      "body_start": 3704,
      "body_end": 3836,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2021/5/30/sri-lanka-launches-probe-after-burning-ship-pollutes-beaches",
        "https://www.marineinsight.com/shipping-news/x-press-pearl-owners-face-legal-action-after-blazing-ship-pollutes-sri-lankan-waters/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00023",
      "text": "IT professional Buvini Liyanagamage tweets:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 23,
      "body_start": 3838,
      "body_end": 3881,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-737865-b00024",
      "text": "This kicked off a debate on the country’s legal framework for such matters. Kamanthi Wickramasinghe argued in an Oped on the Daily Mirror Online that Sri Lanka lacks a proper legal framework and preventive strategies to tackle a big maritime disaster such as this.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 24,
      "body_start": 3883,
      "body_end": 4147,
      "source_links": [
        "http://www.dailymirror.lk/news-features/Claiming-compensation-for-X-Press-Pearl-inferno-Can-the-existing-legal-framework-do-justice/131-213292"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    }
  ],
